{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1114","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Trailing Loves (or L'oeufs?)"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The number \"zero\" is called \"love\" (or \"l'oeuf\" to be precise, literally means \"egg\" in French), for example when denoting the zero score in a game of tennis. "}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aki is fond of numbers, especially those with trailing zeros. For example, the number $$$9200$$$ has two trailing zeros. Aki thinks the more trailing zero digits a number has, the prettier it is."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"However, Aki believes, that the number of trailing zeros of a number is not static, but depends on the base (radix) it is represented in. Thus, he considers a few scenarios with some numbers and bases. And now, since the numbers he used become quite bizarre, he asks you to help him to calculate the beauty of these numbers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$b$$$ (in decimal notation), your task is to calculate the number of trailing zero digits in the $$$b$$$-ary (in the base/radix of $$$b$$$) representation of $$$n\\,!$$$ ("},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Factorial"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"factorial"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$n$$$). "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of the input contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$b$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^{18}$$$, $$$2 \\le b \\le 10^{12}$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print an only integer — the number of trailing zero digits in the $$$b$$$-ary representation of $$$n!$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6 9\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"38 11\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 10\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, $$$6!_{(10)} = 720_{(10)} = 880_{(9)}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third and fourth example, $$$5!_{(10)} = 120_{(10)} = 1111000_{(2)}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The representation of the number $$$x$$$ in the $$$b$$$-ary base is $$$d_1, d_2, \\ldots, d_k$$$ if $$$x = d_1 b^{k - 1} + d_2 b^{k - 2} + \\ldots + d_k b^0$$$, where $$$d_i$$$ are integers and $$$0 \\le d_i \\le b - 1$$$. For example, the number $$$720$$$ from the first example is represented as $$$880_{(9)}$$$ since $$$720 = 8 \\cdot 9^2 + 8 \\cdot 9 + 0 \\cdot 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can read more about bases "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radix"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"here"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1114C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1114/problem/C"}